  "lines": [
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Congratulations, how far along are you now?"},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "Twenty eight weeks, and the pain at the front of my pelvis has got really bad."},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "Turning over in bed is the worst, and getting out of the car."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Any tingling, or changes going to the toilet?"},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "Going to the toilet is fine, more often than normal, but I reckon that's just the baby."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Let me have a look. It's tender right over the pubic bone, and standing on one leg brings it on."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "This looks like pelvic girdle pain, which is really common in pregnancy and usually settles after the birth."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Keep your knees together when you roll over or get in the car, like your legs are tied with a ribbon."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "I'll fit you with a support belt today, wear it whenever you're up and about."},
    {"role": "patient", "text": "Will it harm the baby?"},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "Not at all, it's completely safe."},
    {"role": "clinician", "text": "See you next week."}
  ],
